    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="10, 10a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 10, 10a</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="10" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="258" ed="#robertson"/>Si hom fait plaie [a] auter e il deive faire les amendes, primereinement lui rende sien leche[feo]. E li plaez jurra sur seinz que pur meins nel pot feire ne pur haur si cher nel fist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="259" ed="#robertson"/>If a man wounds another and has to pay compensation, he shall, in the first instance, pay the cost of his medical attendance. And the wounded man shall swear on the holy relics that he could not do it for less, and that he has not increased the amount out of malice.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_14-3">Leis Wl 14.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="409"><label>based on</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-Prol">Af</ref> <quote>interspersed with Alfred's injury-list</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 258–259 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added; Robertson's 10; Liebermann divides it into 10 and 10a (at E li plaez jurra).</note>
      </div>
    </body>
